const HORIZON_ASOF='2026-11-03';
const THESES=[{"id":"russian-avantgarde","t":"Rarity pays, but only for the proven","thesis":"The money will keep concentrating on the few dozen Russian avant-garde works with unbroken Western provenance, as Popova’s October 2026 record showed. With Russian buyers and consignors shut out since 2022 and the fakes problem unresolved, the school trades as scarce Western modernism, not as a national market.","horizon":"10–30 years","dir":"heat","evidence":[{"f":"Popova’s Painterly Architectonic (1918) made £6.2m hammer (£7.6m with fees) at Christie’s London on 14 October 2026, over three times its £1.8m low estimate and nearly four times her 2007 record.","src":[["The Art Newspaper, 15 Oct 2026","https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2026/10/15/christies-achieves-%c2%a3219m-in-steady-solid-london-sales"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"Kandinsky’s Das bunte Leben (1907), restituted in June 2023 to the Lewenstein heirs, sold for £27m hammer (£31.6m with fees) in the same sale, above its £25m high estimate and third-party guaranteed.","src":[["The Art Newspaper, 15 Oct 2026","https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2026/10/15/christies-achieves-%c2%a3219m-in-steady-solid-london-sales"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"Kandinsky’s record is Murnau mit Kirche II (1910), £37.2m ($44.55m) at Sotheby’s London on 1 March 2023, a restituted work; the previous record was £33m ($39.7m) in 2017.","src":[["CNN via ABC17, 3 Mar 2023","https://abc17news.com/entertainment/cnn-style/2023/03/03/kandinsky-painting-recovered-by-holocaust-victims-heirs-sets-auction-record-at-nearly-45-million/"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"Christie’s, Sotheby’s and Bonhams cancelled their June 2022 London Russian sales; Russian art sales at the two majors’ London rooms were £37.7m ($49.6m) in 2021, under 1% of turnover (Art Market Research).","src":[["Reuters via The Business Standard, 17 Mar 2022","https://www.tbsnews.net/node/386558"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"The authenticity problem is on the record: Russian critics challenged Ghent’s museum over dubious avant-garde works (28 Feb 2018), Museum Ludwig tested 22 falsely attributed works (2020) and French authorities seized avant-garde paintings believed stolen (2 Apr 2024).","src":[["The Art Newspaper keyword page: Russian avant-garde","https://www.theartnewspaper.com/keywords/russian-avant-garde"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"An adviser in the room called the Popova result ‘probably not a surprise because her work is so rare’; the article names no buyer and describes no wider Russian avant-garde demand.","src":[["The Art Newspaper, 15 Oct 2026","https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2026/10/15/christies-achieves-%c2%a3219m-in-steady-solid-london-sales"]],"vf":"S"}],"risks":["Fakes: the 2018 Ghent (Toporovski) affair and the 2020 Museum Ludwig review keep buyers to works with pre-1990 Western exhibition history, which shrinks the tradable pool further.","Sanctions: the Russian buyer and consignor base is absent and may stay so; a thaw would add supply before it added demand.","Supply is in museums: the great works sit in the Tretyakov, the Russian Museum, the Stedelijk and MoMA; what trades is mostly works on paper and the odd restituted canvas.","Restitution-driven supply (both 2023 and 2026 Kandinsky records) is lumpy and cannot be planned for."],"record":{"artist":"Wassily Kandinsky","work":"Murnau mit Kirche II (1910)","price":"£37.2m ($44.55m)","house":"Sotheby’s London","date":"2023-03-01","src":[["CNN via ABC17, 3 Mar 2023","https://abc17news.com/entertainment/cnn-style/2023/03/03/kandinsky-painting-recovered-by-holocaust-victims-heirs-sets-auction-record-at-nearly-45-million/"]],"vf":"S","note":"Day inferred from ‘Wednesday’ in an article dated 3 March 2023. Goncharova’s record was not opened in this session."},"movements":["russianavantgarde","expressionism"],"artists":["Liubov Popova","Wassily Kandinsky","Kazimir Malevich","Natalia Goncharova","Alexander Rodchenko","El Lissitzky","Alexandra Exter"],"places":["London","New York"]},{"id":"soviet-nonconformists","t":"Nonconformists wait for a saleroom to return","thesis":"Soviet nonconformist and 20th-century Russian art lost its Western saleroom when London’s Russian Week stopped in 2022; prices now form in a thin private and online trade. Over twenty years the case is museum-led rediscovery of Kabakov, Bulatov, Rabin and Weisberg, but until a major house relists the category the terminal reads it as cool with a long option attached.","horizon":"20–30 years","dir":"cool","evidence":[{"f":"Christie’s, Sotheby’s and Bonhams cancelled their June 2022 Russian art sales in London; Christie’s cited the war and the legal and logistical demands of sanctions, calling its Russian market ‘relatively small’.","src":[["Reuters via The Business Standard, 17 Mar 2022","https://www.tbsnews.net/node/386558"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"In the last full Russian Week, MacDougall’s sold £4.4m on 10 June 2021, with Bulatov’s The Vault of Heaven (2007) at £645,000 the most expensive contemporary work across four London houses that week; Christie’s took £3.1m in Russian paintings.","src":[["USA Art News, 12 Jun 2021","https://usaartnews.com/auctions/macdougall-s-russian-art-auction-success-2"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"Most MacDougall’s lots in June 2021 went to first-time buyers bidding over the internet, which is where the category now lives.","src":[["USA Art News, 12 Jun 2021","https://usaartnews.com/auctions/macdougall-s-russian-art-auction-success-2"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"An American adviser’s 2022 verdict, ‘you don’t want to be caught buying something coming from a Russian at this point’, still describes the compliance reflex at the major houses.","src":[["Reuters via The Business Standard, 17 Mar 2022","https://www.tbsnews.net/node/386558"]],"vf":"S"}],"risks":["Compliance: any consignor or buyer with Russian links triggers sanctions screening, so the houses avoid the category rather than price it.","No price discovery: without London’s twice-yearly sales there is no public benchmark, and private prices can be stale or inflated.","Provenance: Soviet-era export and the 1990s diaspora trade leave gaps that a museum acquisitions committee will query.","The thesis depends on Western museums re-reading the period; the current state of their buying was not established in this session."],"record":{"artist":"Erik Bulatov","work":"The Vault of Heaven (2007)","price":"£645,000","house":"MacDougall’s, London","date":"2021-06-10","src":[["USA Art News, 12 Jun 2021","https://usaartnews.com/auctions/macdougall-s-russian-art-auction-success-2"]],"vf":"S","note":"A sale-week high, not the category record; Kabakov’s record (Beetle, Phillips London, 2008) is carried from memory and was not opened (U). MacDougall’s current sale calendar was not established."},"movements":["conceptual","pop"],"artists":["Ilya Kabakov","Erik Bulatov","Oscar Rabin","Vladimir Weisberg","Komar and Melamid"],"places":["London","Moscow"]},{"id":"indian-modern","t":"India: a domestic market with national-treasure walls","thesis":"Indian modern art will keep rising on domestic wealth, with records set in Mumbai and New Delhi rather than New York. Because the ‘national treasure’ artists cannot leave India, the top of the market is a closed pool of Indian buyers; the Progressives, who can travel, are the international play.","horizon":"10–30 years","dir":"heat","evidence":[{"f":"Raja Ravi Varma’s Yashoda and Krishna (1890s) made $15m hammer, $17.9m with fees (₹167.2 crore) at Saffronart Mumbai on 1 April 2026, against an $8.6–12.9m estimate, bought by Cyrus Poonawalla; a record for an Indian painting.","src":[["The Art Newspaper, 2 Apr 2026","https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2026/04/02/vaccine-billionaire-buys-179m-raja-ravi-varma-setting-new-record-for-indian-painting-at-auction"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"M.F. Husain’s Gram Yatra made $13.7m with fees at Christie’s New York in March 2025; Christie’s New York South Asian sale of 25 March 2026 made $27m, the highest for such a sale outside India, and Sotheby’s New York (24 March 2026) made $22.1m with best prices for 12 artists.","src":[["The Art Newspaper, 2 Apr 2026","https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2026/04/02/vaccine-billionaire-buys-179m-raja-ravi-varma-setting-new-record-for-indian-painting-at-auction"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"Saffronart’s 25th-anniversary sale in New Delhi on 27 September 2025 made Rs 355.77 crore from 85 lots, all sold: Gaitonde’s Untitled (1970) Rs 67.08 crore (artist record), Tyeb Mehta’s Trussed Bull (1956) Rs 56.4 crore, Husain’s Mahabharata Rs 21.6 crore, Souza Rs 20.4 crore, Raza Rs 18 crore.","src":[["PTI via The Week, 28 Sep 2025","https://www.theweek.in/wire-updates/national/2025/09/28/lst3-dl-art-auction.html"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"Ravi Varma is one of the artists designated ‘national treasure’ under India’s 1972 antiquities and art treasures law, so his works cannot leave the country; the buyer could not have been from overseas. Christie’s plans its first live South Asian Modern sale in London in seven years.","src":[["The Art Newspaper, 2 Apr 2026","https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2026/04/02/vaccine-billionaire-buys-179m-raja-ravi-varma-setting-new-record-for-indian-painting-at-auction"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"The September 2025 total beat Saffronart’s April 2025 record by more than 60%, and the house called it ‘a new benchmark for the Indian art market’.","src":[["PTI via The Week, 28 Sep 2025","https://www.theweek.in/wire-updates/national/2025/09/28/lst3-dl-art-auction.html"]],"vf":"S"}],"risks":["The top of the market is a handful of Indian industrialists; a change in their appetite moves prices more than any global trend.","Export rules: national-treasure artists and anything over 100 years old cannot leave India, so foreign buyers are confined to the Progressives and later work.","Rupee weakness turns rupee records into flat dollar results.","Husain and Souza were prolific; attribution and condition questions grow with prices.","Annual national auction totals and the state of the new museums (KNMA’s Adjaye building, NMACC) were not confirmed in this session."],"record":{"artist":"Raja Ravi Varma","work":"Yashoda and Krishna (1890s)","price":"₹167.2 crore ($17.9m with fees; $15m hammer)","house":"Saffronart, Mumbai","date":"2026-04-01","src":[["The Art Newspaper, 2 Apr 2026","https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2026/04/02/vaccine-billionaire-buys-179m-raja-ravi-varma-setting-new-record-for-indian-painting-at-auction"]],"vf":"S"},"movements":["indianmodern","academic"],"artists":["Raja Ravi Varma","M.F. Husain","V.S. Gaitonde","Tyeb Mehta","Amrita Sher-Gil","S.H. Raza","F.N. Souza"],"places":["Mumbai","New Delhi","New York","London"]},{"id":"korean-dansaekhwa","t":"Korea: a bottom forming beneath Dansaekhwa","thesis":"Korean auctions rose in 2025 for the first time in four years but remain well under half their 2021 peak, so Dansaekhwa and the post-war masters are bought at a discount to 2021–22 rather than at a top. Over ten to thirty years Frieze Seoul’s institutional traffic and museum placements argue for a steady re-rating led by Kim Whanki, Yoo Youngkuk, Park Seo-Bo and Lee Ufan.","horizon":"10–30 years","dir":"steady","evidence":[{"f":"Eight Korean auction houses sold 131.5bn won through November 2025, up 16.6%, the first rise in four years; domestic hammer totals had peaked at 324.2bn won in 2021, and the whole Korean art market fell from 806.6bn won (2022) to 615.1bn won (2024).","src":[["Asia Economic Daily, 29 Dec 2025","https://www.asiae.co.kr/en/article/2025122908362226644"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"Lots fell 20% to 8,782 while eight works passed 1bn won (five in 2024); Chagall’s Bouquet de Fleurs at 9.4bn won was the highest price ever at a Korean domestic auction, and Lee Ufan’s Cow and Child made 3.52bn won (2025).","src":[["Asia Economic Daily, 29 Dec 2025","https://www.asiae.co.kr/en/article/2025122908362226644"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"Frieze Seoul 2026 (closed 5 September) had 130+ galleries, 70,000 visitors and 178 museums; Kukje sold a 1971 Yoo Youngkuk for KRW 2.2–2.5bn ($1.6–1.8m), the highest price for a Korean artist at the fair since 2022; White Cube sold two Park Seo-Bo works at $300,000 and $190,000.","src":[["Frieze, Frieze Seoul 2026 report","https://www.frieze.com/article/frieze-seoul-2026-asia-art-market-sales-prizes-acquisitions"]],"vf":"V"},{"f":"Kim Whanki’s 19-VI-71 #206 (1971) made $8.4m at Christie’s New York in November 2025 (estimate $7.5–10m); he holds the top five Korean prices, led by 05-IV-71 #200 (Universe) at HK$88m ($11.3m) at Christie’s Hong Kong in 2019.","src":[["Asia News Network / The Korea Herald, 20 Nov 2025","https://asianews.network/painting-by-south-korean-artist-kim-whan-ki-fetches-8-4-million-at-christies-new-york-auction/"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"South Korea’s art sales rose 6% in 2025 (Arts Economics), against Japan at −1%.","src":[["Art Basel & UBS Art Market Report 2026 (Arts Economics)","https://theartmarket.artbasel.com/download/The-Art-Basel-and-UBS-Art-Market-Report-2026-by-Arts-Economics.pdf"]],"vf":"V"},{"f":"Of 154 Korean galleries and fairs surveyed in December 2025, 48.4% reported lower 2025 sales and 27.1% expected a further fall in 2026; the auction rebound has not yet reached the primary market.","src":[["Asia Economic Daily, 29 Dec 2025","https://www.asiae.co.kr/en/article/2025122908362226644"]],"vf":"S"}],"risks":["The won and the Korean economy drive the domestic bid; galleries expect a flat 2026.","Dansaekhwa supply is large: long careers, series production and late works dilute the scarcity premium.","Kim Whanki’s top prices are set in Hong Kong and New York, not Seoul; the Korean saleroom’s own record is a Chagall.","Western demand for Dansaekhwa after the 2014–16 wave is unproven at the top end."],"record":{"artist":"Kim Whanki","work":"05-IV-71 #200 (Universe) (1971)","price":"HK$88m ($11.3m) as reported","house":"Christie’s Hong Kong","date":"2019-11-23","src":[["Asia News Network / The Korea Herald, 20 Nov 2025","https://asianews.network/painting-by-south-korean-artist-kim-whan-ki-fetches-8-4-million-at-christies-new-york-auction/"]],"vf":"S","note":"The source gives the year only; the day is from memory (U). The price with premium is commonly cited as HK$102m ($13.2m); unresolved here."},"movements":["dansaekhwa","monoha"],"artists":["Kim Whanki","Park Seo-Bo","Lee Ufan","Yoo Youngkuk","Ha Chong-hyun","Yun Hyong-keun","Kim Tschang-yeul"],"places":["Seoul","Hong Kong","New York"]},{"id":"chinese-modern-contemporary","t":"China: big, flat, and splitting in two","thesis":"China is the world’s third market at $8.5bn but grew only about 1% in 2025 while its contemporary auction value fell 18%; the money has moved to Hong Kong evening sales and to a short list of mainland names. The terminal expects the Franco-Chinese moderns (Zao, Sanyu, Chu) to hold as blue chips, the 1990s contemporaries to lag, and the new mainland painters to be the volatile growth.","horizon":"10–30 years","dir":"steady","evidence":[{"f":"China’s art sales were $8.5bn in 2025, up just over 1%, a 14% global share (down one point); mainland auctions rose while Hong Kong contracted.","src":[["Art Basel & UBS Art Market Report 2026 (Arts Economics)","https://theartmarket.artbasel.com/download/The-Art-Basel-and-UBS-Art-Market-Report-2026-by-Arts-Economics.pdf"]],"vf":"V"},{"f":"Contemporary auction sales in China fell 18% in the year to June 2026, though it stayed the second-largest market with about 40 million-dollar results, mainly in Hong Kong and Beijing.","src":[["Artprice Contemporary Art Market Report 2026, release of 8 Oct 2026 via UNI/PRNewswire","https://www.uniindia.com/prnewswire/artprice-releases-its-33rd-annual-contemporary-art-market-report-for-2026-record-transactions-price/207130"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"In 2025 Chinese modern and contemporary art made HK$1.598bn at Christie’s Hong Kong, HK$745m at Sotheby’s Hong Kong and RMB 686m at China Guardian Beijing (about 70% of the market between them); 91 lots passed 10m, 69 of them in Hong Kong.","src":[["Artpro, 2025 China Modern and Contemporary Art Market Report, Part 1","https://share.artpro.com/explore_share/b2/50/b2509758212c64746f8bd631c5c1aea7.html"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"Mainland highs of 2025: Zhang Peili’s X? (1980) RMB 71.3m at China Guardian on 10 November, Huang Yuxing RMB 36.8m (13 May), Zeng Fanzhi RMB 14.03m at Yongle, Liu Ye RMB 10.35m; Zao Wou-Ki’s 1.12.81 made HK$27.6m at Poly Hong Kong in the spring.","src":[["Artpro, 2025 China Modern and Contemporary Art Market Report, Part 1","https://share.artpro.com/explore_share/b2/50/b2509758212c64746f8bd631c5c1aea7.html"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"Christie’s Hong Kong 20th/21st Century autumn sales of 26–27 September 2025 made $105.5m, 96% sold by lot, led by Picasso’s Buste de femme at $25.4m (an Asia record); Greater China led the bidding and new buyers were 20%, over half of them millennials.","src":[["ArtDependence, 29 Sep 2025 (Christie’s release)","https://artdependence.com/articles/christies-hong-kong-20th21st-century-autumn-sales-total-us-106m/"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"Since 5 May 2023 China’s National Cultural Heritage Administration has kept a restricted-export list of works by artists who died after 1911, in eight categories including painting and calligraphy; for listed artists all works or their representative works may not leave China.","src":[["China Justice Observer on the NCHA notice of 5 May 2023","https://www.chinajusticeobserver.com/a/china-imposes-export-curbs-on-artworks-by-certain-authors-who-passed-away-after-1911"]],"vf":"S"}],"risks":["Export curbs: works by listed deceased artists bought on the mainland cannot be exported, and the list can grow; Hong Kong remains the only exit.","Capital controls and the property slump cap mainland bidding; Hong Kong’s own total contracted in 2025.","The 2000s contemporaries (Political Pop, Cynical Realism) depend on a Western demand that has not returned.","Zao Wou-Ki’s record and the Hong Kong autumn 2026 totals by house were not opened in this session."],"record":{"artist":"Zao Wou-Ki","work":"Juin-Octobre 1985","price":"HK$510m (≈$65m)","house":"Sotheby’s Hong Kong","date":"2018-09-30","src":[],"vf":"U","note":"Carried from memory and the brief; no page opened in this session. The 2025 marker with a source is Zhang Peili’s RMB 71.3m at China Guardian (S)."},"movements":["chinesecontemporary"],"artists":["Zao Wou-Ki","Sanyu","Chu Teh-Chun","Zeng Fanzhi","Liu Ye","Zhang Peili","Huang Yuxing"],"places":["Hong Kong","Beijing","Shanghai"]},{"id":"chinese-ink-classical","t":"Classical Chinese: the oldest money, the deepest bids","thesis":"Classical painting, calligraphy and works of art are where Chinese wealth bid hardest through the downturn: a Yuan handscroll made HK$250m in 2025 and Sotheby’s Asian works-of-art series was its most valuable since 2013. Supply is finite and keeps moving into museums, so the terminal expects records to keep falling at the top while the middle stays thin.","horizon":"10–30 years","dir":"heat","evidence":[{"f":"A Yuan dynasty handscroll by Rao Jie sold for HK$250m ($32m) at Sotheby’s Hong Kong in 2025, 25 times its estimate after more than 200 bids, the most valuable Chinese calligraphy sold at the house.","src":[["Sotheby’s, Asian Art 2025 in review","https://www.sothebys.com/en/articles/inside-a-stellar-year-for-asian-art-at-sothebys-2025-in-review"]],"vf":"V"},{"f":"Sotheby’s autumn 2025 Asian Art series in Hong Kong made HK$1.4bn ($180.37m); the Asian Works of Art series alone made HK$1.17bn ($150m), the most valuable since 2013, with the Ise ceramics collection 99.5% sold and a Southern Song Guan dish at HK$55.88m.","src":[["Sotheby’s, Asian Art 2025 in review","https://www.sothebys.com/en/articles/inside-a-stellar-year-for-asian-art-at-sothebys-2025-in-review"]],"vf":"V"},{"f":"The Xiao Wan Liu Tang fan paintings and calligraphy made HK$182.32m ($23.46m) across three sales, led by Yun Shouping’s Landscape after Zhao Mengfu at HK$11.6m; the season drew the highest number of new bidders in 14 years, from 20 regions.","src":[["Sotheby’s, Asian Art 2025 in review","https://www.sothebys.com/en/articles/inside-a-stellar-year-for-asian-art-at-sothebys-2025-in-review"]],"vf":"V"},{"f":"Mainland auction sales rose in 2025 while Hong Kong contracted, within a Chinese market of $8.5bn (+1%).","src":[["Art Basel & UBS Art Market Report 2026 (Arts Economics)","https://theartmarket.artbasel.com/download/The-Art-Basel-and-UBS-Art-Market-Report-2026-by-Arts-Economics.pdf"]],"vf":"V"},{"f":"The NCHA’s May 2023 restricted-export list covers calligraphy and painting by named artists who died after 1911; older material falls under China’s cultural-relics export regime.","src":[["China Justice Observer on the NCHA notice of 5 May 2023","https://www.chinajusticeobserver.com/a/china-imposes-export-curbs-on-artworks-by-certain-authors-who-passed-away-after-1911"]],"vf":"S"}],"risks":["Anything deemed a cultural relic cannot leave the mainland; the buyer’s liquidity is Hong Kong or nothing.","Attribution: scrolls, seals and colophons are the most forged objects in the Chinese market, and the top prices rest on connoisseurship rather than science.","Poly and China Guardian 2025–26 totals for classical painting were not established in this session; the mainland top end is known here only through Hong Kong.","A mainland economic or political shock would hit this segment first, since its buyers are domestic."],"record":{"artist":"Qi Baishi","work":"Twelve Landscape Screens (1925)","price":"RMB 931.5m (≈$140.8m)","house":"Poly Auction, Beijing","date":"2017-12-17","src":[],"vf":"U","note":"The terminal’s own record entry; not opened in this session. The sourced 2025 marker is the Rao Jie handscroll, HK$250m at Sotheby’s Hong Kong (V), day not given by the source."},"movements":["chineseink"],"artists":["Qi Baishi","Zhang Daqian","Fu Baoshi","Xu Beihong","Rao Jie","Yun Shouping"],"places":["Hong Kong","Beijing"]},{"id":"middle-east-modern","t":"Gulf money, Arab moderns: the re-rating begins","thesis":"Arab and Iranian modernism is priced far below its museum presence: the top Arab lot of 2023 was $1.1m and Mahmoud Saïd’s 2010 record of $2.43m still stands. With Christie’s and Sotheby’s now selling in Abu Dhabi and Riyadh and the Guggenheim Abu Dhabi opening in December 2026, the terminal expects a decade of catching up, led by state and foundation buying.","horizon":"10–30 years","dir":"heat","evidence":[{"f":"Mahmoud Saïd’s Les Chadoufs (1934) made $2.43m against a $150,000–200,000 estimate at Christie’s Dubai in April 2010, the most expensive work by an Arab artist the house had sold there; the sale made about $15.1m, 86% sold.","src":[["Haute Living, 28 Apr 2010","https://hauteliving.com/2010/04/egyptian-artist-mahmoud-said-brings-in-a-record-2-43-million-at-christies-dubai-sale/42554/"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"The ten most expensive Arab works of 2023 ran from $352,800 (Etel Adnan) to $1.1m (Mohammed Al Saleem, a Saudi record, Sotheby’s, October 2023), with Saïd’s Fille à l’imprimé at $721,849 from the Dalloul collection in November 2023.","src":[["The National, 31 Dec 2023","https://www.thenationalnews.com/arts-culture/art-design/2023/12/31/arab-artworks-auction-christies-sothebys"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"Sotheby’s Origins II in Riyadh (January 2026) made $19.5m; Safeya Binzagr’s Coffee Shop in Madina Road sold for $2.1m against a projected $1.05–1.35m, and about a third of lots went to local buyers.","src":[["Arab News","https://www.arabnews.pk/node/2636560"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"A Saudi adviser says regional artists ‘still trade at 15 to 30 percent of Western peers’ with comparable museum representation; Qantara puts Middle Eastern collectors at 23% of global demand for contemporary works above $1m.","src":[["Arab News","https://www.arabnews.pk/node/2636560"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"Christie’s first Abu Dhabi fine-art sale, Mawasim, on 1 November 2026 offered 70 Middle Eastern works spanning nine decades, with lenders including Sharjah’s Barjeel Art Foundation and Beirut’s Dalloul collection; the Guggenheim Abu Dhabi opens on 11 December 2026.","src":[["The National, 30 Oct 2026","https://thenationalnews.com/arts-culture/art-design/2026/10/30/abu-dhabi-is-gaining-ground-in-the-art-market-says-christies-ceo"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"The counter-signal: Middle East contemporary auction sales fell 28% in the year to June 2026, largely in the Gulf (Artprice).","src":[["Artprice Contemporary Art Market Report 2026, release of 8 Oct 2026 via UNI/PRNewswire","https://www.uniindia.com/prnewswire/artprice-releases-its-33rd-annual-contemporary-art-market-report-for-2026-record-transactions-price/207130"]],"vf":"S"}],"risks":["Regional war: the Gulf sales run in the shadow of conflict and a single escalation empties the room.","State and foundation demand can stop as quickly as it started; private Gulf collectors remain few.","The great collections (Barjeel, Dalloul, Mathaf) lend rather than sell, so the secondary supply is thin and often minor.","Authentication bodies for Saïd, Guiragossian and the Baghdad moderns are young; fakes follow prices."],"record":{"artist":"Mahmoud Saïd","work":"Les Chadoufs (1934)","price":"$2.43m","house":"Christie’s Dubai","date":"2010-04-27","src":[["Haute Living, 28 Apr 2010","https://hauteliving.com/2010/04/egyptian-artist-mahmoud-said-brings-in-a-record-2-43-million-at-christies-dubai-sale/42554/"]],"vf":"S","note":"Day inferred from ‘last night’ in an article dated 28 April 2010. No higher price for an Arab modern was found in this session; Christie’s Abu Dhabi results of 1 November 2026 were not opened (see unconfirmed)."},"movements":["expressionism","realism"],"artists":["Mahmoud Saïd","Paul Guiragossian","Monir Shahroudy Farmanfarmaian","Etel Adnan","Shakir Hassan Al Said","Safeya Binzagr","Samia Halaby","Mohammed Al Saleem"],"places":["Abu Dhabi","Riyadh","Dubai","Doha","London"]},{"id":"gulf-salerooms","t":"Abu Dhabi and Riyadh become sale rooms","thesis":"Within thirty years the Gulf will be the third saleroom region after New York–London and Hong Kong: Christie’s held its first Abu Dhabi fine-art sale on 1 November 2026, Sotheby’s sells in Riyadh and opens in Abu Dhabi in December, and the Guggenheim Abu Dhabi opens on 11 December 2026. Museums are the demand; the open question is whether private Gulf wealth follows them.","horizon":"10–30 years","dir":"heat","evidence":[{"f":"Christie’s chief executive Bonnie Brennan, in Abu Dhabi for the 1 November 2026 sale, said ‘the market can sustain two centres’ and that the house would ‘love to have a more regularly scheduled calendar of sales’ there; Rothko, Kandinsky and Picasso lots were shown in Abu Dhabi before their New York sales.","src":[["The National, 30 Oct 2026","https://thenationalnews.com/arts-culture/art-design/2026/10/30/abu-dhabi-is-gaining-ground-in-the-art-market-says-christies-ceo"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"Christie’s first-half 2026 auction sales were $3.5bn, up 71%, and millennials and Gen Z were 47% of its new clients; the Abu Dhabi season also brings Frieze’s first fair in November and the Guggenheim opening on 11 December 2026.","src":[["The National, 30 Oct 2026","https://thenationalnews.com/arts-culture/art-design/2026/10/30/abu-dhabi-is-gaining-ground-in-the-art-market-says-christies-ceo"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"Saudi Arabia targets culture at about 3% of GDP by 2030 (roughly SR180bn, $48bn) from SR60bn in 2023; about 20 museums are planned, the Saudi Museum of Contemporary Art has opened and Colnaghi is opening in Riyadh.","src":[["Arab News","https://www.arabnews.pk/node/2636560"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"Saudi private wealth exceeds $2.4trn but Saudi buyers were 0.01% of high-value art purchases, and Saudi family offices put about 1% into art against about 7% globally (Qantara); Sotheby’s Origins II in Riyadh (January 2026) made $19.5m.","src":[["Arab News","https://www.arabnews.pk/node/2636560"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"Middle East contemporary auction sales fell 28% in the year to June 2026, largely in the Gulf (Artprice), so the new rooms open into a soft regional cycle.","src":[["Artprice Contemporary Art Market Report 2026, release of 8 Oct 2026 via UNI/PRNewswire","https://www.uniindia.com/prnewswire/artprice-releases-its-33rd-annual-contemporary-art-market-report-for-2026-record-transactions-price/207130"]],"vf":"S"}],"risks":["War in the region is the dominant risk to every Gulf date on the calendar.","Demand is state-led; a budget turn in Riyadh or Abu Dhabi would remove the marginal bidder.","Four hubs (Abu Dhabi, Dubai, Riyadh, Doha) compete for the same collectors and lenders, which can dilute each of them.","Import, VAT and free-port rules for the new rooms, and the results of Christie’s 1 November sale and Art Basel Qatar, were not opened in this session."],"record":{"artist":"Safeya Binzagr","work":"Coffee Shop in Madina Road","price":"$2.1m","house":"Sotheby’s, Riyadh (Origins II)","date":"2026-01","src":[["Arab News","https://www.arabnews.pk/node/2636560"]],"vf":"S","note":"The source gives January 2026 only, and does not call it a record; the previous Saudi record cited was Al Saleem’s $1.1m (2023)."},"movements":[],"artists":["Monir Shahroudy Farmanfarmaian","Samia Halaby","Nabil Nahas","Safeya Binzagr","Mohammed Al Saleem"],"places":["Abu Dhabi","Riyadh","Doha","Dubai"]},{"id":"latin-american","t":"Latin America: Surrealism’s women lead a re-rating","thesis":"Kahlo’s $54.7m in November 2025 made a Latin American the most expensive woman artist at auction, and the Surrealist collections sold around her went white-glove. With Brazilian galleries up 21% in 2025 and SP-Arte growing, the terminal expects Mexican and Brazilian modernism to re-rate over two decades, though the supply of Kahlo and Tarsila is tiny and partly locked at home.","horizon":"10–30 years","dir":"heat","evidence":[{"f":"Kahlo’s El sueño (La cama) (1940) made $47m hammer, $54.6m with fees (reported as $54.7m) at Sotheby’s New York on 20 November 2025, above a $40m low estimate, passing O’Keeffe’s $44.4m (2014) as the record for a woman artist and for a Latin American work.","src":[["The Art Newspaper, 21 Nov 2025","https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2025/11/21/frida-kahlo-record-van-gogh-still-life-sothebys-auction-new-york"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"The 24-lot ‘Exquisite Corpus’ Surrealist collection made $98m with fees (estimate $66.7–98.9m), all sold, with 11 of 24 lots above high estimate and records for Dorothea Tanning ($2.7m hammer), Bellmer and Paalen; Sotheby’s Helena Newman cited ‘the surge in interest in the movement in the last several years’.","src":[["The Art Newspaper, 21 Nov 2025","https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2025/11/21/frida-kahlo-record-van-gogh-still-life-sothebys-auction-new-york"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"SP-Arte’s 22nd edition (8–12 April 2026, São Paulo) had over 180 galleries, studios and institutions; the Art Basel and UBS report records a 21% rise in Brazilian galleries’ 2025 sales, and the fair’s design section grew from 23 to 64 stands since 2016.","src":[["The Art Newspaper, 10 Apr 2026","https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2026/04/10/sp-arte-underscores-latin-americas-resilient-rise-amid-global-market-recalibration"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"The New York Times noted that O’Keeffe’s 2014 price is about $60.5m in today’s money, so the Kahlo record is a nominal, not a real, high for a woman artist.","src":[["The Art Newspaper, 21 Nov 2025","https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2025/11/21/frida-kahlo-record-van-gogh-still-life-sothebys-auction-new-york"]],"vf":"S"}],"risks":["Mexico treats Kahlo and Rivera as national patrimony, so works inside Mexico do not come to New York; the auction supply is the pre-war diaspora of pictures and little else.","Brazil’s and Mexico’s currencies and politics set the local bid; the Brazilian gallery rise is one year of data.","Carrington’s $28.5m (2024), Tarsila’s and Botero’s records were not opened in this session and are carried as unconfirmed.","The Surrealism wave since the 2024 centenary can crest; the 2025 records came from two single-owner collections."],"record":{"artist":"Frida Kahlo","work":"El sueño (La cama) (1940)","price":"$54.7m with fees ($47m hammer)","house":"Sotheby’s New York","date":"2025-11-20","src":[["The Art Newspaper, 21 Nov 2025","https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2025/11/21/frida-kahlo-record-van-gogh-still-life-sothebys-auction-new-york"]],"vf":"S"},"movements":["surrealism","mexicanmuralism"],"artists":["Frida Kahlo","Leonora Carrington","Remedios Varo","Tarsila do Amaral","Fernando Botero","Diego Rivera","Carmen Herrera"],"places":["New York","Mexico City","São Paulo"]},{"id":"african-modern-contemporary","t":"Africa: 0.1% of the market, after the boom","thesis":"African art is about 0.1% of global auction value and its 2020–22 stars fell with the under-40 segment, down 26.6% in the year to June 2026. The long case rests on museums (Tate buying Boafo at 1-54, MOWAA in Benin City) and on the moderns, Enwonwu, Stern, Sekoto, El Anatsui, whose supply is finite; the terminal reads cool now, warming over twenty years.","horizon":"20–30 years","dir":"cool","evidence":[{"f":"African art is roughly $72m a year at auction against a $67.8bn global market, about 0.1% (ArtTactic figures as cited); Strauss & Co’s year was R475.5m (about $26m) and its Nairobi sale about $230,000, 86% sold.","src":[["MoMAA, Where is Africa in the 2025 auction records?","https://momaa.org/where-is-africa-in-the-2025-auction-records/"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"Julie Mehretu’s Walkers With the Dawn and Morning made $10.7m at Sotheby’s New York in November 2023, the highest auction price for an African-born artist; Akunyili Crosby reached $4.74m (2022), El Anatsui $2.2m, Enwonwu’s Tutu $1.67m (2018), and Irma Stern’s Malay (Black Headdress) (1946) R21.7m (about $1.26m) at Strauss & Co.","src":[["MoMAA, Where is Africa in the 2025 auction records?","https://momaa.org/where-is-africa-in-the-2025-auction-records/"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"Auction sales of artists under 40 fell 26.6% in the year to June 2026 while contemporary art overall rose 6%; Artprice says the correction is ‘bringing prices back toward more sustainable levels’.","src":[["Artprice Contemporary Art Market Report 2026, release of 8 Oct 2026 via UNI/PRNewswire","https://www.uniindia.com/prnewswire/artprice-releases-its-33rd-annual-contemporary-art-market-report-for-2026-record-transactions-price/207130"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"Tate acquired an Amoako Boafo painting at 1-54 Marrakech in early 2025; at Christie’s London on 14 October 2026 Portia Zvavahera set a record at £307,200 and Igshaan Adams sold at £96,000.","src":[["MoMAA, Where is Africa in the 2025 auction records?","https://momaa.org/where-is-africa-in-the-2025-auction-records/"],["The Art Newspaper, 15 Oct 2026","https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2026/10/15/christies-achieves-%c2%a3219m-in-steady-solid-london-sales"]],"vf":"S"}],"risks":["Infrastructure: few auction houses, weak currencies (rand, naira) and costly shipping keep most trade in London, New York and Paris.","The 2020–22 cohort (Boafo and peers) was bought for resale; its price fall since 2021 was not quantified in this session.","Records cluster in three Western salerooms’ themed sales, which can be cut when totals fall.","Export and heritage rules in Nigeria and South Africa for the moderns were not established here."],"record":{"artist":"Julie Mehretu","work":"Walkers With the Dawn and Morning (2008)","price":"$10.7m","house":"Sotheby’s New York","date":"2023-11-15","src":[["MoMAA, Where is Africa in the 2025 auction records?","https://momaa.org/where-is-africa-in-the-2025-auction-records/"]],"vf":"S","note":"The source gives November 2023; the day is from memory (U)."},"movements":["africanmodern","ultracontemporary"],"artists":["Julie Mehretu","El Anatsui","Ben Enwonwu","Irma Stern","Gerard Sekoto","Amoako Boafo","Njideka Akunyili Crosby","Portia Zvavahera"],"places":["London","New York","Lagos","Cape Town","Marrakech"]},{"id":"southeast-asian-japanese","t":"Japan and Vietnam: Asia’s next blue chips","thesis":"Hong Kong’s autumn 2026 sales put Japanese and Vietnamese pictures at the top: Nara’s Present made HK$71.7m, Japanese artists sold 100%, and Vu Cao Dam set the Vietnamese record at HK$29m. With Kusama’s death closing her supply and Foujita entering single-artist sales, the terminal expects Japan to anchor Asian demand and Vietnamese and Indonesian moderns to re-rate over two decades.","horizon":"10–30 years","dir":"heat","evidence":[{"f":"At Sotheby’s Hong Kong on 28 September 2026 Nara’s Present (1994) made HK$71.66m ($9.32m) and The Crated Room in Iceland/Drawing Room (2009) HK$61.9m; Japanese artists sold 100% across both evening sales.","src":[["Sotheby’s, 2 Oct 2026","https://www.sothebys.com/en/articles/editorial-sothebys-hong-kong-evening-auction-total-hits-three-year-high"]],"vf":"V"},{"f":"Vu Cao Dam’s Conversation d’élégantes au jardin (1939) made HK$28.96m ($3.76m) after 14 bids, the highest price for a Vietnamese work at auction; Tetsuya Ishida’s Can’t Fly Anymore (1996) made HK$12.16m above its high estimate.","src":[["Sotheby’s, 2 Oct 2026","https://www.sothebys.com/en/articles/editorial-sothebys-hong-kong-evening-auction-total-hits-three-year-high"]],"vf":"V"},{"f":"The Foujita Lexicon (Lewis collection) was a white-glove sale at HK$67.2m ($8.74m), Sotheby’s first single-artist auction in Asia; Kusama’s Infinity-Nets (LHLUJ) (2017) made HK$15.36m ($2.0m), above its high estimate.","src":[["Sotheby’s, 2 Oct 2026","https://www.sothebys.com/en/articles/editorial-sothebys-hong-kong-evening-auction-total-hits-three-year-high"]],"vf":"V"},{"f":"A year earlier Nara’s Can’t Wait ’til the Night Comes (2012) made HK$79.9m at Sotheby’s Hong Kong (28 September 2025), and at Christie’s Hong Kong that week Thai, Vietnamese, Filipino, Japanese and Korean artists sold 100%.","src":[["Artpro, 2025 China Modern and Contemporary Art Market Report, Part 1","https://share.artpro.com/explore_share/b2/50/b2509758212c64746f8bd631c5c1aea7.html"],["ArtDependence, 29 Sep 2025 (Christie’s release)","https://artdependence.com/articles/christies-hong-kong-20th21st-century-autumn-sales-total-us-106m/"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"Utamaro’s Fukagawa in Snow made HK$55.27m ($7.1m) in 2025, a record for the artist and for ukiyo-e painting, and the Okada Museum of Art sale made HK$688m ($88m) over 125 lots.","src":[["Sotheby’s, Asian Art 2025 in review","https://www.sothebys.com/en/articles/inside-a-stellar-year-for-asian-art-at-sothebys-2025-in-review"]],"vf":"V"},{"f":"Yayoi Kusama died in August 2026 aged 97; the effect on her prices is not yet measurable.","src":[],"vf":"U"}],"risks":["Concentration: two artists, Nara and Kusama, carry most of the Japanese total; Kusama’s very large supply of prints and late works can swamp the scarcity effect of her death.","Vietnamese and Indonesian moderns have a long fakes history (Hanoi school, Affandi), and few catalogues raisonnés.","Japan’s own market is flat (−1% in 2025); the demand is Hong Kong and Chinese money, not Tokyo.","Gutai, Affandi, Hendra Gunawan and Le Pho records were not opened in this session."],"record":{"artist":"Vu Cao Dam","work":"Conversation d’élégantes au jardin (1939)","price":"HK$28.96m ($3.76m)","house":"Sotheby’s Hong Kong","date":"2026-09-28","src":[["Sotheby’s, 2 Oct 2026","https://www.sothebys.com/en/articles/editorial-sothebys-hong-kong-evening-auction-total-hits-three-year-high"]],"vf":"V","note":"Record for a Vietnamese work. Nara’s own record (Knife Behind Back, Sotheby’s Hong Kong, 2019) was not opened (U)."},"movements":["gutai","superflat","ukiyoe"],"artists":["Yoshitomo Nara","Yayoi Kusama","Tsuguharu Foujita","Vu Cao Dam","Le Pho","Affandi","Kazuo Shiraga","Tetsuya Ishida"],"places":["Hong Kong","Tokyo","Singapore"]},{"id":"women-artists","t":"Women artists: from discount to premium","thesis":"Women are now 45% of the artists dealers show and 37% of dealer sales by value, and the records of 2025–26 (Kahlo $54.7m; Popova, Riley and Hepworth in one October week) came from scarcity meeting museum re-reading. The terminal expects the gap to male peers to keep closing for thirty years, fastest for modernists with small, catalogued bodies of work.","horizon":"10–30 years","dir":"heat","evidence":[{"f":"In 2025 women were 45% of artists represented by dealers (up 4 points) and 37% of dealer sales by value (up 2); primary-market galleries made 44% of sales from women’s work.","src":[["Art Basel & UBS Art Market Report 2026 (Arts Economics)","https://theartmarket.artbasel.com/download/The-Art-Basel-and-UBS-Art-Market-Report-2026-by-Arts-Economics.pdf"]],"vf":"V"},{"f":"Kahlo’s El sueño (La cama) made $54.7m with fees at Sotheby’s New York on 20 November 2025, the record for a woman artist, passing O’Keeffe’s $44.4m of 2014; Dorothea Tanning set a record at $2.7m hammer the same night.","src":[["The Art Newspaper, 21 Nov 2025","https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2025/11/21/frida-kahlo-record-van-gogh-still-life-sothebys-auction-new-york"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"On 14 October 2026 Christie’s London set records for Popova (£7.6m with fees), Bridget Riley (£5.2m with fees), Hepworth as a painter (£537,600) and Portia Zvavahera (£307,200).","src":[["The Art Newspaper, 15 Oct 2026","https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2026/10/15/christies-achieves-%c2%a3219m-in-steady-solid-london-sales"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"Li Hei Di set a record at HK$3.33m after 18 bids at Sotheby’s Hong Kong on 28 September 2026, and Safeya Binzagr’s Coffee Shop in Madina Road made $2.1m at Sotheby’s Riyadh in January 2026.","src":[["Sotheby’s, 2 Oct 2026","https://www.sothebys.com/en/articles/editorial-sothebys-hong-kong-evening-auction-total-hits-three-year-high"],["Arab News","https://www.arabnews.pk/node/2636560"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"At Frieze Seoul 2026 Lehmann Maupin placed a Kim Yun Shin painting with a Korean museum and David Zwirner placed two Mamma Andersson paintings with a South Korean museum.","src":[["Frieze, Frieze Seoul 2026 report","https://www.frieze.com/article/frieze-seoul-2026-asia-art-market-sales-prizes-acquisitions"]],"vf":"V"}],"risks":["‘Women artists’ is a basket, not a school; the index rises because of a few estates (Kahlo, Mitchell, Carrington) and can fall with them.","In real terms the ceiling has barely moved: O’Keeffe’s 2014 price is about $60.5m today, above the Kahlo record.","The ultra-contemporary women of 2021–22 sit inside the under-40 segment, down 26.6% in the year to June 2026.","Saville’s 2025 show and record, and the Mitchell, Krasner and Agnes Martin records, were not opened in this session."],"record":{"artist":"Frida Kahlo","work":"El sueño (La cama) (1940)","price":"$54.7m with fees ($47m hammer)","house":"Sotheby’s New York","date":"2025-11-20","src":[["The Art Newspaper, 21 Nov 2025","https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2025/11/21/frida-kahlo-record-van-gogh-still-life-sothebys-auction-new-york"]],"vf":"S"},"movements":["surrealism","russianavantgarde","abex"],"artists":["Frida Kahlo","Liubov Popova","Bridget Riley","Barbara Hepworth","Joan Mitchell","Lee Krasner","Agnes Martin","Leonora Carrington","Jenny Saville"],"places":["New York","London","Paris"]},{"id":"sculpture-design","t":"Sculpture: estates sell, speculation does not","thesis":"Three-dimensional work now splits by provenance: Lalanne’s estate sold 70 animals for $58.9m in October 2024 with 97% of lots above high estimate, Hepworth led Christie’s Modern British week in October 2026, but the unguaranteed $70m Giacometti stalled at $64m in May 2025. The terminal expects collectible design and fresh estates to keep gaining share, while trophy bronzes need a guarantor.","horizon":"10–30 years","dir":"steady","evidence":[{"f":"Christie’s New York sold 70 François-Xavier Lalanne sculptures from Dorothée Lalanne on 10 October 2024 for $58.9m, 97% of lots above their high estimates; Très Grand Centaure (2001) made $7.5m against a $1.2m high estimate and Très Grand Ours (2009) $6.1m.","src":[["Artnet News, Oct 2024","https://news.artnet.com/market/christies-francois-xavier-lalanne-auction-nets-59-million-2552168"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"Lalanne bidders came 54% from the Americas, 15% from Asia Pacific and 31% from Europe; his record remains Léopard I (2001) at $9.6m in 2021.","src":[["Artnet News, Oct 2024","https://news.artnet.com/market/christies-francois-xavier-lalanne-auction-nets-59-million-2552168"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"Giacometti’s Grande tête mince (1954/55), estimated above $70m and unguaranteed, stalled at about $64m and failed to sell at Sotheby’s New York on 13 May 2025; the Modern evening sale made $186.4m with fees against a $170–248m estimate, 83% sold, with 26 of the sold lots guaranteed.","src":[["The Art Newspaper, 14 May 2025","https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2025/05/14/70m-giacometti-bombs-at-patchy-sothebys-impressionist-and-modern-art-sale"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"The same night a Frank Lloyd Wright lamp made almost $7.5m with fees after an 11-minute bidding war, a record for Wright, and a smaller Giacometti sold within estimate at $6.8m with fees.","src":[["The Art Newspaper, 14 May 2025","https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2025/05/14/70m-giacometti-bombs-at-patchy-sothebys-impressionist-and-modern-art-sale"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"Hepworth set a painting record of £537,600 at Christie’s London on 14 October 2026; at Frieze Seoul 2026 Thaddaeus Ropac sold an Antony Gormley for $1m.","src":[["The Art Newspaper, 15 Oct 2026","https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2026/10/15/christies-achieves-%c2%a3219m-in-steady-solid-london-sales"],["Frieze, Frieze Seoul 2026 report","https://www.frieze.com/article/frieze-seoul-2026-asia-art-market-sales-prizes-acquisitions"]],"vf":"S"}],"risks":["Editions and posthumous casts: for Giacometti, Rodin and Lalanne the cast, the number and the foundry decide the price, and estates can add supply.","Lalanne’s run is partly fashion (the Jacquemus staging); design cycles turn faster than painting cycles.","Sculpture’s share of auction turnover (Artprice) could not be read in this session; the Hepworth sculpture record of 21 October 2026 and Giacometti’s $141.3m record were not opened.","Trophy lots without guarantees have failed in public, which deters consignors and pushes them to private sales."],"record":{"artist":"François-Xavier Lalanne","work":"Très Grand Centaure (2001)","price":"$7.5m","house":"Christie’s New York","date":"2024-10-10","src":[["Artnet News, Oct 2024","https://news.artnet.com/market/christies-francois-xavier-lalanne-auction-nets-59-million-2552168"]],"vf":"S","note":"Top lot of the Dorothée Lalanne sale, not the artist’s record (Léopard I, $9.6m, 2021). The sculpture record, Giacometti’s L’Homme au doigt ($141.3m, Christie’s New York, 11 May 2015), is in the terminal and was not opened here (U)."},"movements":["surrealism","pop"],"artists":["Alberto Giacometti","François-Xavier Lalanne","Barbara Hepworth","Louise Bourgeois","Ruth Asawa","Constantin Brâncuși","Jeff Koons"],"places":["New York","London","Paris"]},{"id":"old-masters","t":"Old Masters: scarcity, one buyer, and sleepers","thesis":"The Old Master market is thin but its top is firm because the great names are nearly all in museums: a re-identified Rembrandt made £6.75m in December 2025 and went to Thomas Kaplan’s Leiden Collection, his 18th, and a Rembrandt lion drawing made nearly $18m in February 2026. The terminal expects the few tradable masterworks to rise with Gulf and Asian museum building while the middle market keeps shrinking.","horizon":"10–30 years","dir":"steady","evidence":[{"f":"Rembrandt’s Saint John on Patmos (c.1661), long thought to show his son Titus, sold at Sotheby’s London in December 2025 for £6.75m (about $9m); the buyer, revealed on 28 September 2026, was Thomas Kaplan, and it is the 18th Rembrandt the Leiden Collection has acquired in about two decades.","src":[["The Art Newspaper, 28 Sep 2026","https://theartnewspaper.com/2026/09/28/rembrandt-painting-buyer-revealed-leiden-collection-thomas-kaplan"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"Kaplan’s Rembrandt drawing Young Lion Resting (c.1638–42) made nearly $18m at Sotheby’s New York in February 2026, against a November 2025 expectation of about $15m; the proceeds endow the Panthera wildlife charity.","src":[["The Art Newspaper, 28 Sep 2026","https://theartnewspaper.com/2026/09/28/rembrandt-painting-buyer-revealed-leiden-collection-thomas-kaplan"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"Kaplan attributes the strength of Rembrandt masterworks to ‘extreme scarcity’, allows that his buying may affect prices ‘in specific moments’, and sellers now expect him to bid, which can push prices up.","src":[["The Art Newspaper, 28 Sep 2026","https://theartnewspaper.com/2026/09/28/rembrandt-painting-buyer-revealed-leiden-collection-thomas-kaplan"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"Across fine art, 56% of offline auction value in 2025 came from lots of $1m or more, while online-only sales fell to $9.2bn, the lowest since 2019; the top is where the Old Master money sits.","src":[["Art Basel & UBS Art Market Report 2026 (Arts Economics)","https://theartmarket.artbasel.com/download/The-Art-Basel-and-UBS-Art-Market-Report-2026-by-Arts-Economics.pdf"]],"vf":"V"}],"risks":["Attribution risk runs both ways: a sleeper can be upgraded (the Saint John) or a bought picture downgraded by a scholar’s committee.","One-buyer dependence: if Kaplan stops bidding, the Rembrandt market loses its floor.","Export licensing in the UK, Italy and France can stop a sale or delay it for years; the Gulf and Asian museums that would buy are abroad.","Old Master sale totals for 2025–26 were not established in this session; the Salvator Mundi record is in the terminal, not opened here."],"record":{"artist":"Rembrandt van Rijn","work":"Saint John on Patmos (c.1661)","price":"£6.75m (about $9m)","house":"Sotheby’s London","date":"2025-12-04","src":[["The Art Newspaper, 28 Sep 2026","https://theartnewspaper.com/2026/09/28/rembrandt-painting-buyer-revealed-leiden-collection-thomas-kaplan"]],"vf":"S","note":"Not a record: a 2025–26 marker. The Old Master record, Salvator Mundi at $450.3m (Christie’s New York, 15 Nov 2017), is in the terminal (U here). The day comes from the 4 December 2025 report the article links."},"movements":["dutchgolden","baroque","highren"],"artists":["Rembrandt van Rijn","Johannes Vermeer","Peter Paul Rubens","Frans Hals"],"places":["London","New York","Amsterdam","Abu Dhabi"]},{"id":"ultra-contemporary","t":"Ultra-contemporary: the correction is the opportunity","thesis":"Artists under 40 lost 26.6% of auction value in the year to June 2026 while the rest of contemporary rose 6%, and Artprice calls the correction a return to sustainable prices. The terminal expects the 2020–22 cohort to trade below its peaks for a decade; the thirty-year winners will be the few with museum shows, so buying should follow institutions, not auction momentum.","horizon":"10 years, then 30","dir":"cool","evidence":[{"f":"Contemporary art (artists born after 1945) rose 6% in auction value and 9% in volume in the year to 30 June 2026, after three years of decline, with a record number of lots sold for the sixth year; the roughly $100m gain was all recorded in the United States.","src":[["Artprice Contemporary Art Market Report 2026, release of 8 Oct 2026 via UNI/PRNewswire","https://www.uniindia.com/prnewswire/artprice-releases-its-33rd-annual-contemporary-art-market-report-for-2026-record-transactions-price/207130"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"Sales of artists under 40 fell 26.6% in the same year and the gap to the rest of the market widened; the market ‘returned decisively to growth’ without higher prices.","src":[["Artprice Contemporary Art Market Report 2026, release of 8 Oct 2026 via UNI/PRNewswire","https://www.uniindia.com/prnewswire/artprice-releases-its-33rd-annual-contemporary-art-market-report-for-2026-record-transactions-price/207130"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"Artprice’s annual report of 10 March 2026 says market stability now ‘rests primarily on lower-priced transactions’, that galleries are fragile with closures and restructuring, and that millennial and Gen Z buyers compare prices online and favour affordable works.","src":[["Artprice, The Art Market Report 2025 (Spanish edition), 10 Mar 2026","https://news.artprice.com/es/13754/the-art-market-report-2025-by-artprice-the-long-awaited-recovery-appears-to-have-begun"]],"vf":"V"},{"f":"Young names still clear at modest levels: at Sotheby’s Hong Kong on 28 September 2026 Li Hei Di set a record at HK$3.33m with 18 bids and Yu Nishimura’s at night (2022) made HK$2.3m, over double its high estimate.","src":[["Sotheby’s, 2 Oct 2026","https://www.sothebys.com/en/articles/editorial-sothebys-hong-kong-evening-auction-total-hits-three-year-high"]],"vf":"V"},{"f":"Online-only sales, the channel that carried the 2021 boom, fell to $9.2bn in 2025, 15% of the market and the lowest since 2019.","src":[["Art Basel & UBS Art Market Report 2026 (Arts Economics)","https://theartmarket.artbasel.com/download/The-Art-Basel-and-UBS-Art-Market-Report-2026-by-Arts-Economics.pdf"]],"vf":"V"}],"risks":["A new speculative cohort (Asian millennial favourites, AI-themed painting) can repeat the 2021 cycle before the last one has cleared.","Dealers’ waiting lists and resale clauses hide the true price fall; auction is the visible fraction.","The Bank of America figure of young contemporary 88% below its 2022 peak is in the terminal and was not opened here.","Museum validation is slow and uneven; following institutions means paying up once the show is announced."],"record":{"artist":"Li Hei Di","work":"Untitled (2023)","price":"HK$3,328,000 ($432,640)","house":"Sotheby’s Hong Kong","date":"2026-09-28","src":[["Sotheby’s, 2 Oct 2026","https://www.sothebys.com/en/articles/editorial-sothebys-hong-kong-evening-auction-total-hits-three-year-high"]],"vf":"V","note":"A current artist record, cited as the marker of the segment’s new price level; the 2021–22 records (Boafo, Yukhnovich, Weyant) were not opened."},"movements":["ultracontemporary"],"artists":["Amoako Boafo","Jadé Fadojutimi","Flora Yukhnovich","Anna Weyant","Li Hei Di","Yu Nishimura","Lucy Bull"],"places":["New York","London","Hong Kong"]},{"id":"primary-market-dealers","t":"Dealers: flat sales, fairs up, online down","thesis":"Dealer sales were $34.8bn in 2025, up 2%, with a third of galleries selling less, online down to 16% of their turnover and fairs up to 35%. The terminal expects the primary market to keep consolidating around fairs and the largest galleries for a decade, which favours buying from estates and from the lists institutions are buying rather than from first shows.","horizon":"10 years","dir":"cool","evidence":[{"f":"Dealer sales were an estimated $34.8bn in 2025, up 2%; 42% of dealers reported higher sales, 33% lower and 25% stable; dealers above $10m grew 3%, and those under $500,000 saw double-digit rises in average sale values.","src":[["Art Basel & UBS Art Market Report 2026 (Arts Economics)","https://theartmarket.artbasel.com/download/The-Art-Basel-and-UBS-Art-Market-Report-2026-by-Arts-Economics.pdf"]],"vf":"V"},{"f":"Online was 16% of dealer turnover in 2025 (down 6 points) while art fairs rose to 35% of dealer sales from 31%; public auction sales rose 9% but auction houses’ private sales fell 5%.","src":[["Art Basel & UBS Art Market Report 2026 (Arts Economics)","https://theartmarket.artbasel.com/download/The-Art-Basel-and-UBS-Art-Market-Report-2026-by-Arts-Economics.pdf"]],"vf":"V"},{"f":"Artprice (10 March 2026) describes galleries as fragile, with closures and restructuring, and auction houses adapting through revised estimates, more selective offerings and more private sales.","src":[["Artprice, The Art Market Report 2025 (Spanish edition), 10 Mar 2026","https://news.artprice.com/es/13754/the-art-market-report-2025-by-artprice-the-long-awaited-recovery-appears-to-have-begun"]],"vf":"V"},{"f":"Frieze Seoul 2026 drew 178 museums and institutions from 25 countries, a fair record, and sales of $1m or more by Hauser & Wirth, Almine Rech, Ropac and Pace; David Zwirner’s James Green said ‘the buying power in the region remains strong’.","src":[["Frieze, Frieze Seoul 2026 report","https://www.frieze.com/article/frieze-seoul-2026-asia-art-market-sales-prizes-acquisitions"]],"vf":"V"},{"f":"Regional contrasts: Brazilian galleries’ sales rose 21% in 2025, while 48.4% of Korean galleries and fairs reported lower sales.","src":[["The Art Newspaper, 10 Apr 2026","https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2026/04/10/sp-arte-underscores-latin-americas-resilient-rise-amid-global-market-recalibration"],["Asia Economic Daily, 29 Dec 2025","https://www.asiae.co.kr/en/article/2025122908362226644"]],"vf":"S"}],"risks":["Fair costs and mega-gallery concentration squeeze the middle, which is where new artists are first priced.","Gallery closures cut off primary supply for emerging artists and strand their collectors without a market-maker.","UBS flags geopolitical, tariff and cost risks for 2026; a US tariff on art would hit the fair circuit first.","The dealer figures are a survey of respondents, not a census."],"record":{"artist":"Yoo Youngkuk","work":"Untitled (1971)","price":"KRW 2.2–2.5bn ($1.6–1.8m)","house":"Kukje Gallery at Frieze Seoul","date":"2026-09-05","src":[["Frieze, Frieze Seoul 2026 report","https://www.frieze.com/article/frieze-seoul-2026-asia-art-market-sales-prizes-acquisitions"]],"vf":"V","note":"A fair sale, not an auction: the highest price for a Korean artist at Frieze Seoul since its 2022 launch. The date is the fair’s closing day; the report gives a range, as dealers do."},"movements":["ultracontemporary","dansaekhwa"],"artists":["Yoo Youngkuk","Rashid Johnson","Adrian Ghenie","Gerhard Richter"],"places":["Seoul","São Paulo","Basel","New York"]},{"id":"asia-salerooms","t":"Hong Kong holds; Seoul and Tokyo bid","thesis":"Hong Kong’s autumn 2026 evening sale rose 35% to HK$739m, its best since 2023, with Asia records for Renoir and Matisse and the most new bidders in 14 years, while Seoul’s auctions rose 16.6% in 2025 and Frieze Seoul drew 178 museums. The terminal expects Hong Kong to remain Asia’s saleroom for twenty years, with Seoul and Tokyo as the fairs where new money is met first.","horizon":"10–30 years","dir":"steady","evidence":[{"f":"Sotheby’s Hong Kong Modern and Contemporary evening auction of 28 September 2026 made HK$738.55m ($96.0m), up 35% on the previous season and the category’s highest Hong Kong total since autumn 2023; Renoir (HK$52.14m) and Matisse (HK$21.03m) set Asia records.","src":[["Sotheby’s, 2 Oct 2026","https://www.sothebys.com/en/articles/editorial-sothebys-hong-kong-evening-auction-total-hits-three-year-high"]],"vf":"V"},{"f":"Sotheby’s autumn 2025 Asian Art season drew the highest number of new bidders in 14 years, from 20 regions, and the house transacted over $346.83m of Asian art worldwide in 2025.","src":[["Sotheby’s, Asian Art 2025 in review","https://www.sothebys.com/en/articles/inside-a-stellar-year-for-asian-art-at-sothebys-2025-in-review"]],"vf":"V"},{"f":"Christie’s Hong Kong 20th/21st Century sales of 26–27 September 2025 made $105.5m, 96% sold by lot, with Picasso’s Buste de femme at $25.4m an Asia record; bidders came from 32 countries and new buyers were 20%.","src":[["ArtDependence, 29 Sep 2025 (Christie’s release)","https://artdependence.com/articles/christies-hong-kong-20th21st-century-autumn-sales-total-us-106m/"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"China’s $8.5bn market (+1%) saw Hong Kong contract in 2025 while the mainland rose; South Korea grew 6% and Japan fell 1%.","src":[["Art Basel & UBS Art Market Report 2026 (Arts Economics)","https://theartmarket.artbasel.com/download/The-Art-Basel-and-UBS-Art-Market-Report-2026-by-Arts-Economics.pdf"]],"vf":"V"},{"f":"Korean auctions sold 131.5bn won through November 2025 (+16.6%), the first rise in four years, and Frieze Seoul 2026 had 70,000 visitors from 54 countries and 178 museums, its highest figures to date.","src":[["Asia Economic Daily, 29 Dec 2025","https://www.asiae.co.kr/en/article/2025122908362226644"],["Frieze, Frieze Seoul 2026 report","https://www.frieze.com/article/frieze-seoul-2026-asia-art-market-sales-prizes-acquisitions"]],"vf":"V"}],"risks":["Hong Kong carries political and legal risk that New York and London do not; a shock would move the Asian saleroom to Singapore or Tokyo faster than any fair could.","The Asia records are for Western names (Picasso, Renoir, Matisse), which tells where Asian money goes, not that Asian schools are being re-rated.","Tokyo (Art Week Tokyo, Sotheby’s Tokyo), Singapore (Art SG) and Shanghai’s bonded zone were not researched in this session.","Mainland capital controls cap the Hong Kong bid; the 2025 contraction shows it."],"record":{"artist":"Pablo Picasso","work":"Buste de femme (1944)","price":"$25.4m","house":"Christie’s Hong Kong","date":"2025-09-26","src":[["ArtDependence, 29 Sep 2025 (Christie’s release)","https://artdependence.com/articles/christies-hong-kong-20th21st-century-autumn-sales-total-us-106m/"]],"vf":"S","note":"Asia auction record for Picasso; cited as the saleroom marker, not a school record. Sale held 26–27 September 2025."},"movements":["chinesecontemporary","dansaekhwa","superflat"],"artists":["Pablo Picasso","Pierre-Auguste Renoir","Henri Matisse","Yoshitomo Nara","Marc Chagall"],"places":["Hong Kong","Seoul","Tokyo","Singapore","Shanghai"]},{"id":"figurative-return","t":"The figure returns: stories outsell surfaces","thesis":"The money of 2025–26 has gone to pictures with people in them: Kahlo’s bed, Nara’s child, Ravi Varma’s Yashoda, Binzagr’s coffee shop, Hurvin Anderson’s Last House and the Surrealist collections that sold white-glove. The terminal reads a fifty-year swing back from process and surface to narrative, portraiture and myth, which favours the figurative moderns of every region over the next thirty years.","horizon":"10–30 years","dir":"heat","evidence":[{"f":"Sotheby’s three New York sales of 20 November 2025 made $304.5m with fees, all sold; Kahlo’s self-portrait in bed made $54.7m and the 24-lot Surrealist ‘Exquisite Corpus’ collection $98m, with records for Tanning, Bellmer and Paalen.","src":[["The Art Newspaper, 21 Nov 2025","https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2025/11/21/frida-kahlo-record-van-gogh-still-life-sothebys-auction-new-york"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"At Christie’s London on 14 October 2026 Bacon’s Figure in Movement (1978) led at £17.2m with fees and Hurvin Anderson’s Last House (2013) made £5.7m with fees, more than double its £2m low estimate after bidding among three phone bidders.","src":[["The Art Newspaper, 15 Oct 2026","https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2026/10/15/christies-achieves-%c2%a3219m-in-steady-solid-london-sales"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"In Hong Kong on 28 September 2026 two Nara figure paintings made HK$71.66m and HK$61.9m, Ishida’s Can’t Fly Anymore beat its high estimate and the figurative Foujita single-artist sale sold 100%.","src":[["Sotheby’s, 2 Oct 2026","https://www.sothebys.com/en/articles/editorial-sothebys-hong-kong-evening-auction-total-hits-three-year-high"]],"vf":"V"},{"f":"Ravi Varma’s mythological Yashoda and Krishna made $17.9m in Mumbai on 1 April 2026; DAG’s Ashish Anand spoke of ‘a growing recognition of mythology as a serious and desirable genre within the global art market’.","src":[["The Art Newspaper, 2 Apr 2026","https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2026/04/02/vaccine-billionaire-buys-179m-raja-ravi-varma-setting-new-record-for-indian-painting-at-auction"]],"vf":"S"},{"f":"The counter-evidence is also strong: Mondrian’s Composition III made £25.2m the same London night, Kusama’s Infinity-Nets beat its estimate in Hong Kong, and a Yuan calligraphy scroll made HK$250m in 2025.","src":[["The Art Newspaper, 15 Oct 2026","https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2026/10/15/christies-achieves-%c2%a3219m-in-steady-solid-london-sales"],["Sotheby’s, Asian Art 2025 in review","https://www.sothebys.com/en/articles/inside-a-stellar-year-for-asian-art-at-sothebys-2025-in-review"]],"vf":"S"}],"risks":["Taste cycles are long but not permanent; abstraction’s top prices (Rothko, Mondrian, Kandinsky) remain above most figurative records.","The figurative boom of 2020–22 in young painting is the segment now down 26.6%; the swing favours proven moderns, not new names.","Surrealism’s run since the 2024 centenary rests on a few single-owner collections.","A ‘fifty-year’ reading cannot be tested on two seasons of data."],"record":{"artist":"Yoshitomo Nara","work":"Present (1994)","price":"HK$71.66m ($9.32m)","house":"Sotheby’s Hong Kong","date":"2026-09-28","src":[["Sotheby’s, 2 Oct 2026","https://www.sothebys.com/en/articles/editorial-sothebys-hong-kong-evening-auction-total-hits-three-year-high"]],"vf":"V","note":"Top lot of the night and the highest figurative price of Hong Kong’s autumn 2026; not Nara’s record."},"movements":["surrealism","neoexpressionism","superflat","academic","pop"],"artists":["Frida Kahlo","Yoshitomo Nara","Hurvin Anderson","Raja Ravi Varma","Safeya Binzagr","Francis Bacon","Tetsuya Ishida","Jenny Saville"],"places":["New York","London","Hong Kong","Mumbai"]}];
const HORIZON_SIGNALS=[{"t":"Korea: auctions up, galleries down","dir":"steady","p":"Eight Korean auction houses sold 131.5bn won through November 2025, up 16.6% and the first rise in four years, on 20% fewer lots, with eight works above 1bn won. The market remains far below its 2021 domestic hammer peak of 324.2bn won and the 2022 transaction peak of 806.6bn won. In a December 2025 survey 48.4% of galleries and fairs reported lower sales and 27.1% expect a further fall in 2026.","s":[["Asia Economic Daily, 29 Dec 2025","https://www.asiae.co.kr/en/article/2025122908362226644"]],"vf":"S"},{"t":"India sets its records at home","dir":"heat","p":"Raja Ravi Varma’s Yashoda and Krishna made $17.9m with fees at Saffronart Mumbai on 1 April 2026, a record for an Indian painting, bought by Cyrus Poonawalla because national-treasure status keeps it in India. Saffronart’s 27 September 2025 sale made Rs 355.77 crore, all 85 lots sold, with a Gaitonde record at Rs 67.08 crore. Christie’s New York’s $27m on 25 March 2026 is the most for a South Asian sale outside India.","s":[["The Art Newspaper, 2 Apr 2026","https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2026/04/02/vaccine-billionaire-buys-179m-raja-ravi-varma-setting-new-record-for-indian-painting-at-auction"],["PTI via The Week, 28 Sep 2025","https://www.theweek.in/wire-updates/national/2025/09/28/lst3-dl-art-auction.html"]],"vf":"S"},{"t":"Scarcity pays: a Yuan scroll and a Rembrandt","dir":"heat","p":"A Yuan dynasty handscroll by Rao Jie made HK$250m ($32m) at Sotheby’s Hong Kong in 2025, 25 times its estimate after more than 200 bids, in an Asian works-of-art season worth HK$1.17bn, the most valuable since 2013. In London a re-identified Rembrandt made £6.75m in December 2025 and went to the Leiden Collection, and a Rembrandt drawing made nearly $18m in New York in February 2026. Finite supply, not fashion, set these prices.","s":[["Sotheby’s, Asian Art 2025 in review","https://www.sothebys.com/en/articles/inside-a-stellar-year-for-asian-art-at-sothebys-2025-in-review"],["The Art Newspaper, 28 Sep 2026","https://theartnewspaper.com/2026/09/28/rembrandt-painting-buyer-revealed-leiden-collection-thomas-kaplan"]],"vf":"S"}];
